        "description": "USN-8071-1 fixed a vulnerability in nss. This update provides the corresponding fix for Ubuntu 14.04 LTS, Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that NSS incorrectly handled memory when performing  certain GHASH operations. A remote attacker could use this issue to cause  NSS to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute  arbitrary code.",
